  "decision_summary": "The query is pyridostigmine, a quaternary dimethylcarbamoyl pyridinium. Direct comparative evidence gives pyridostigmine F=7.6%, and the closest analogue neostigmine is 1-2% with one report of 18.9%. These low values outweigh less transferable high F from rivastigmine, which lacks the quaternary charge. Therefore predict low (<20%).",
